# Async/Await Patterns

## Structured Concurrency (Python 3.11+)

- Use `asyncio.TaskGroup` for production code — never `asyncio.gather()`
- TaskGroup auto-cancels all tasks if one fails
- Use `asyncio.timeout()` — never `asyncio.wait_for()`

## Concurrency Control

- Use `asyncio.Semaphore` to bound concurrency
- Tune to `floor(rate_limit / avg_seconds_per_call / 60)` with 20-30% headroom
- Never run unbounded `gather()` against external APIs

## Error Handling

- Use `tenacity` for exponential backoff with jitter
- Retry only 429 and 5xx — never retry 4xx
- Add jitter: `random.uniform(0, 1)` to prevent thundering herd
- Respect `retry-after` headers

## CPU-Bound Work

- Use `asyncio.to_thread()` for CPU-bound post-processing
- Never call sync blocking code inside `async def`
- Use `def` for CPU-bound; FastAPI runs it in thread pool
